{"id":"theos.sh-b26","title":"Fix phantom hit in marchTerrain coarse→fine transition","description":"## Bug

`src/renderer/ascii-raycast/march.ts:107` sets `prevD = stride` after a coarse
(sphere-trace) jump. `stride` is a positive distance-to-travel, not a signed
distance to the surface. On the next iteration that enters the fine band, the
crossing check at line ~123

  if (prevD > 0 && d <= 0) { ... }

fires on stale data — `prevD > 0` is trivially true because it's a stride
length, so the very first fine step after exiting coarse phase can spuriously
trigger a "crossing." The interpolated hit parameter `k = prevD / (prevD - d)`
ends up outside `[0, 1]` and the returned hit point is displaced from the
actual surface.

## Impact

Phantom hits on near-tangent rays — e.g. rays grazing the inner equator of the
torus, or rays that just skim the bounding sphere and re-enter the fine band
close to the surface. In normal forward-facing views the coarse phase usually
ends well before the fine band, which is why current golden/smoke tests pass.
The hazard is real for grazing-angle and silhouette rendering.

## Fix

After the coarse stride, recompute `prevD` as the true signed distance
(mirror the pre-loop init block at march.ts:88–96):

    const rho2 = Math.sqrt(posX*posX + posY*posY);
    const dr2 = rho2 - R;
    const base2 = Math.sqrt(dr2*dr2 + posZ*posZ) - r;
    if (base2 > fineBand) {
      prevD = base2 - A;
    } else {
      const uA = Math.atan2(posY, posX);
      const vA = Math.atan2(posZ, rho2 - R);
      prevD = base2 - sampleH(((uA/TAU)+1)%1, ((vA/TAU)+1)%1);
    }

## Acceptance

- Add a test that places a ray at near-tangent incidence (e.g. graze the
  inner equator) and asserts the returned hit point lies within linear-
  refinement tolerance of the true surface.
- Existing 301/301 test suite stays green.

