{"id":"theos.sh-6k5","title":"Signal-bus subscriptions leak on scene transition","description":"SurfaceApp.onMount registers all TITLE_SCENE_EFFECTS. On dissolve→walk, only the cell contributors named in TITLE_EFFECTS_TO_UNREGISTER are removed via Applicator.unregister. The underlying signal-bus subscriptions (buildMask, maskReady, frameBegin, buildFields) from reveal, text-mask, manifold-genus, text-cells stay alive for the entire walk scene.

Benign today: reveal's frameBegin handler runs every frame on stale revealedMask but no cell contributor reads it in walk. Latent: any future effect that reacts to these handlers' side effects could break.

